{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/765938-dragon-companions","id":765938,"title":"Dragon Companions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-14T18:30:09-08:00","id":765938,"title":"Dragon Companions?","content":"I have had access to the Scion rpg for many years, but have only recently started playing the game. My friends have looked through multiple source books, but cannot find the stats for a birthright level 5 dragon. Are there rules for creating a dragon? Is there actually a dragon with stats I've missed in one of the books? I would appreciate any help or insightful knowledge on how to handle this situation. All help is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9360-vespor","name":"Vespor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T00:19:40-08:00","id":766116,"title":"","content":"I don't think an actual dragon has appeared in any of the books. <br /> <br /> There are things like linworms (?) which are fake dragons. Wyverns may be in there somewhere too.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you'll have to stat one up yourself. My non-game-based mythology is a little rusty, but there's plenty of stuff on eastern dragons, which would be perfectly fitting for a chinese or japanese scion. The dungeons and dragons style western dragons, like smaug, are mostly from European myth I think, but might fit a Norse scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T06:57:27-08:00","id":766217,"title":"","content":"Well, theres the Tatsu in Demigod, which is a Guide, but still a dragon. My personal suggestion would be that you adapt the Coatl from Hero a bit, make it an ounce stronger and re-style it and voila, you got your dragon. One of the Example Characters basically does the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T08:40:11-08:00","id":766283,"title":"","content":"I believe Nidhog is stated up in Ragnarok, and I'm certain Fafnir (a Svartalfar with power to turn into a dragon) is in there too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T11:43:36-08:00","id":766430,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the suggestions. In the stories they even mention other dragons, but haven't seen stats for one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9360-vespor","name":"Vespor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T18:34:43-08:00","id":766733,"title":"","content":"on the antagonist sections of Demigod there are stats for Ladon, Nidhog, Tatsu and Xiuhcoatl, Tatsu is Stated as a Four dot Guide.<br /> <br /> Fafnir is in that same book and section, it says to use Nidhog stats for his dragon form <br /> <br /> Nidhog himself is said to have 4 children, that are weaker than him, the book tells how to stat this ones lowering their father\u00b4s stats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4856-alfanumerico","name":"alfanumerico","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T16:45:40-08:00","id":767427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vespor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/765938-dragon-companions#post765938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have had access to the Scion rpg for many years, but have only recently started playing the game. My friends have looked through multiple source books, but cannot find the stats for a birthright level 5 dragon. Are there rules for creating a dragon? Is there actually a dragon with stats I've missed in one of the books? I would appreciate any help or insightful knowledge on how to handle this situation. All help is appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Isn't Nidhog from the Norse supposed to be a dragon? Or do they call it a serpent? Also, I think the Chinese god of the sea is a dragon too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T17:47:13-08:00","id":767478,"title":"","content":"You're thinking of Ryujin, who is Japanese and yes a gigantic-size dragon. Sadly they don't give actual stats for him, just a divine parent writeup in God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T20:20:51-08:00","id":767543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/765938-dragon-companions?p=767478#post767478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're thinking of Ryujin, who is Japanese and yes a gigantic-size dragon. Sadly they don't give actual stats for him, just a divine parent writeup in God.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, couldn't remember his name, or I'd have recognized he's Japanese. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Couldn't you tweak the Nemean template a bit to create a dragon? They're already powerful animals and creatures, so it shouldn't be too difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}